<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chahar Lang</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chahar Lang is one of the two main divisions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakhtiari">Bakhtiari</a> tribal confederation of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, the other being the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haft-lang">Haft Lang</a>. Its clans lived mainly in the western parts of Bakhtiari territory in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> mountains. Rivalry between the leading khans of the two divisions shaped Bakhtiari politics, though from the 19th century the Haft Lang khans usually held the paramount chieftainship.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chahar-lang.jpg" alt="Chahar Lang" width="320" height="287" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PayamAvarwand · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bakhtiari-Girls.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
